# Where the Skills Directory app reads its catalog from.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local overrides (`.env.local` is gitignored).

# The registry repo that holds the skills (owner/repo).
SKILLS_REPO=miguel-leca-superside/superside-skills

# Which branch/tag/commit to read.
SKILLS_REPO_REF=main

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRODUCTION (Vercel): set a token and the app fetches skills from GitHub at
# build/revalidate time ("fetch-at-build"). New skills appear on their own.
#
# Create a token with READ access to the private superside-skills repo:
#   GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Fine-grained tokens →
#   Repository access: only superside-skills · Permissions: Contents = Read-only
# Then add it in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables as
# SKILLS_REPO_TOKEN. Do NOT commit a real token.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SKILLS_REPO_TOKEN=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL DEV: if no token is set, the app reads a local checkout of the registry
# instead (no token needed). Defaults to a sibling folder next to this app:
#   ../superside-skills
# Point it elsewhere if your checkout lives somewhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SKILLS_LOCAL_PATH=/absolute/path/to/superside-skills

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WRITE TOKEN — powers "Upload a Skill" (opens a PR into submissions/) and
# "Request a Skill" (opens a GitHub Issue). Without it those flows are disabled
# (the pages still render). A read token (SKILLS_REPO_TOKEN above) is enough to
# LIST requests; this one is needed to CREATE them.
#   GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Fine-grained tokens →
#   Repository access: only superside-skills · Permissions:
#     Contents = R/W · Pull requests = R/W · Issues = R/W
#   Set it in Vercel as SKILLS_SUBMIT_TOKEN. Never commit it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SKILLS_SUBMIT_TOKEN=github_pat_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# METRICS (optional) — powers the "Most viewed" and "Top installed" sorts by
# counting detail-page views and installs (.zip downloads + CLI-command copies)
# in a Redis store over its REST API. Works with Vercel KV or Upstash — both
# speak the same protocol. Without these vars, view/install tracking is a no-op
# and those two sort options are simply hidden (the other sorts still work).
#
# Vercel: add a KV/Upstash integration to the project and it injects
# KV_REST_API_URL + KV_REST_API_TOKEN automatically. Or set them by hand:
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KV_REST_API_URL=https://your-db.upstash.io
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# (UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL / UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN are accepted too.)
